  grid: 8-19 rows x 9-16 cols, uniform background (any non-fg color)
  colors: exactly 2 foreground colors -- line_col (always 1 [observed]) and blocker_col (always 6 [observed])
  segment:
    two endpoint pixels of line_col on a strict 45-degree diagonal (|dr|==|dc|, dr!=0)
    segment length (inclusive): 6-10 cells
    endpoints not on grid edges; at least 1 cell margin from each border
  blockers:
    0-2 pixels of blocker_col placed on interior cells of the segment (not at endpoints)
    the segment must be the unique diagonal pair across ALL fg pixels with the most blockers
  distractors:
    0-5 additional fg pixels (either color) scattered on background
    not on the primary segment, not on any perpendicular diagonal emitted by blockers
    must not form any same-color diagonal pair whose segment contains >= primary's blocker count
  output:
    paint line_col along the entire primary segment (preserving blocker pixels)
    each blocker emits a full perpendicular 45-degree diagonal across the grid in blocker_col
    all distractors remain unchanged

